---
import ProductionLayout from '../layouts/ProductionLayout.astro';
---
<ProductionLayout title="Archive — Skyhook Industries" description="Archived early Skyhook Industries concepts preserved for project history." noindex={true}>
  <section class="page-hero paper-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Archive / project history</p>
    <h1>Early ideas, kept in context.</h1>
    <p>Explore the proposals and research that helped shape Skyhook Industries.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="paper-section">
    <div class="section-grid">
      <p class="chapter-label">Archived concepts</p>
      <div>
        <h2>Preserve the trail.</h2>
        <article class="archive-item" id="mission-proposal">
          <p class="status-label">ARCHIVED CONCEPT — NOT CURRENT ROADMAP</p>
          <h3>Comet 26P / Grigg–Skjellerup mission proposal</h3>
          <p>An early proposal imagined a Skyhook as a first step toward reaching Comet 26P. Its sequence moved from surveying and landing to robotic work with local material, then to a large trajectory change.</p>
          <ol class="archive-sequence">
            <li><b>01 / BUILD</b><span>Develop a working tether before attempting the comet expedition.</span></li>
            <li><b>02 / SURVEY</b><span>Reach 26P, inspect it and identify a place for robotic surface operations.</span></li>
            <li><b>03 / USE LOCAL MATERIAL</b><span>Investigate whether cometary material could support a propulsion system.</span></li>
            <li><b>04 / CHANGE COURSE</b><span>Explore a substantial change to the comet's trajectory toward an Earth encounter.</span></li>
          </ol>
          <p class="archive-caveat">An exploratory proposal from the project's early years; comet operations are not part of the current roadmap.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="paper-section archive-source-section">
    <div class="section-grid">
      <p class="chapter-label">Research lineage</p>
      <div class="archive-source-grid">
        <div>
          <h2>Keep the source in view.</h2>
          <p class="lede">Robert P. Hoyt and Chauncey Uphoff's cislunar tether study is part of the project's research lineage.</p>
          <a class="cta light" href="https://www.niac.usra.edu/files/studies/final_report/7Hoyt.pdf">Read the cislunar tether study ↗</a>
        </div>
        <aside class="archive-folio" aria-label="Cislunar Tether Transport System bibliographic record">
          <span>ARCHIVE / SOURCE 01</span>
          <strong>Cislunar Tether<br />Transport System</strong>
          <p>Robert P. Hoyt · Chauncey Uphoff<br />NASA Institute for Advanced Concepts · 1999</p>
          <small>Research source · 1999</small>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="paper-section" aria-labelledby="early-writing">
    <div class="section-grid">
      <p class="chapter-label">Early tether writing</p>
      <div>
        <h2 id="early-writing">Imagining a different way up.</h2>
        <div class="source-list">
          <a class="source" id="high-wire-act" href="https://frc.ri.cmu.edu/~hpm/project.archive/general.articles/1981/high.wire/high.wire.html">
            <span class="source-type">OMNI</span><div><h3>High Wire Act</h3><p>Robert L. Forward and Hans P. Moravec imagine a passenger journey using an orbital cable, then explain the transportation concept behind the story.</p></div><span class="source-year">1981 ↗</span>
          </a>
          <a class="source" id="orbital-bridges" href="https://frc.ri.cmu.edu/~hpm/project.archive/general.articles/1987/skyhook.ltx">
            <span class="source-type">Hans Moravec · text source</span><div><h3>Orbital Bridges</h3><p>A historical essay comparing synchronous and rotating skyhooks, their material demands and uses around Earth, the Moon and in free space. Opens the original .ltx text source in the author's CMU archive.</p></div><span class="source-year">1986 ↗</span>
          </a>
          <a class="source" id="non-synchronous-skyhook" href="https://frc.ri.cmu.edu/~hpm/project.archive/1976.skyhook/papers/scable.pox">
            <span class="source-type">Astronautical Sciences · manuscript source</span><div><h3>A Non-Synchronous Orbital Skyhook</h3><p>Hans Moravec's rotating-skyhook study, published in the Journal of the Astronautical Sciences, volume 25, issue 4, pages 307–322. Opens the original .pox manuscript source in the author's CMU archive.</p></div><span class="source-year">1977 ↗</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="paper-section">
    <div class="section-grid">
      <p class="chapter-label">Current baseline</p>
      <div>
        <h2>Use the live system pages.</h2>
        <p class="lede">Current architecture, assumptions, research sources and program gates live on the main site and in the repository documentation.</p>
        <a class="cta light" href="/system/">Current system →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</ProductionLayout>
